          "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/bitcoin/bitcoin/git/commits/11090c8bb359f894ef7d97b65aff52fe8191aec1",
          "sha": "11090c8bb359f894ef7d97b65aff52fe8191aec1",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/11090c8bb359f894ef7d97b65aff52fe8191aec1"
        }
      ],
      "message": "wallet, bdbro: Reject revisited btree pages\n\nValidating btree page levels stops a page from being its own ancestor, but\na page can still be reachable from more than one parent while keeping a\nconsistent level. Such a page, and everything below it, is parsed again for\nevery path that reaches it, so a small file can describe an exponential\namount of work. A valid btree references each page once, so keep track of\nthe pages already visited and reject any that is seen again.",
      "committer": {
        "name": "Shuvam Pandey",
        "email": "shuvampandey1@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-08-16T21:11:47Z"
      },
